        text: 'Near the Equator the wind dies. For weeks the ships drift in the <b>doldrums</b> under a burning sun, then are battered by sudden squalls. Sailors see <b>St. Elmo’s fire</b>—glowing electric light dancing on the masts—and take it as a sign of good luck.',
