        text: 'After <b>38 days</b>, you burst out into an endless ocean. Magellan weeps with joy. Because the water is so calm, he names it <b>Mar Pacífico</b>—the Pacific, or “peaceful,” Ocean. No one aboard knows how enormous it really is. You catch fish and fill water casks for the crossing.',
