        text: 'Three years after leaving, the Victoria limps into Sanlúcar with just <b>18 men</b>—out of about 270 who set out. They are the first people ever to sail <b>all the way around the world</b>. The cloves they carry pay for the whole expedition. The world is round—and far bigger than anyone had imagined.',
