    epilogue: 'The voyage proved that all the world’s oceans are connected, that the Earth is far bigger than Columbus believed, and that the Pacific is enormous. <b>Antonio Pigafetta’s</b> journal recorded the peoples, animals and places they encountered. Elcano was given a coat of arms showing a globe and the motto <i>“Primus circumdedisti me”</i>—“You were the first to go around me.”',
    accomplishments: ['Led the first expedition to sail around the world (1519–1522)', 'Found the Strait of Magellan, linking the Atlantic and Pacific', 'Named the Pacific Ocean', 'Proved the Earth is far larger than Europeans believed'],
